+   unstaged hunk was committed. The fix snapshots pre-repair working-tree blobs
+   and stages ONLY the repair's delta by 3-way merge (`git merge-file`).
+2. `test_notice_is_silent_on_commit_a` — `git commit -a` runs the hook with
+   GIT_INDEX_FILE=$GIT_DIR/index.lock, which matched none of the silent
+   patterns, so the "this is a pathspec commit" notice fired, falsely, on a
+   command that is not a pathspec commit. Measured 2026-09-11 in a scratch
+   repository. The locked index BECOMES the real index on commit, so nothing
+   the notice warns about (MM afterwards, content outside the pathspec) is
+   true there.
